{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And Moses said to Hobab.</b> The Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote that Hobab is Jethro, who was given a new name when he returned to the Torah of Israel, for so is the way of every convert — for His servants He calls by a different name — and he is the father of Zipporah, and Reuel was a title of eldership, and Scripture says (Exodus 2:18) ״אל רעואל אביהן,״ just as Jacob said (Genesis 32:10) ״אלהי אבי אברהם,״ and Scripture says of Belshazzar that he is the son of Nebuchadnezzar, when he was his grandson. But the Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted that Jethro had seven names. And regarding what he said, ״I will not go, but to my land and to my birthplace I go״ — Moses entreated him to go with them and said to him simply, ״and we will treat you well,״ and he [Moses] thought to give him from the spoil silver and gold and garments and sheep and cattle, but he would have no inheritance among them, and therefore he [Hobab] did not want this, and he answered, ״but to my land and to my birthplace I go,״ for there I have inheritance and property and honor. Then Moses said to him, ״Please do not leave us, for inasmuch as you know the desert you will be for us as eyes in the conquest of the lands, and you will guide us on the way by which we shall go, and from all the good that HaShem does for us we will do good to you״ — an allusion to giving him an estate and a good land as his reward for his toil and his help when he assists them in conquering the land. And in my opinion he was persuaded by him and did so. Thus far his [Ramban's] language, of blessed memory."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:04.907885401Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}